title: ClearFrame — why the history cannot be edited
---
flowchart LR
    subgraph chain["THE CHAIN — one row per state change"]
        direction LR
        E1["<b>seq 1</b> · Producer<br/>pass_opened<br/><br/>prev = 000…000<br/>hash = <b>a3f1…</b>"]
        E2["<b>seq 2</b> · Script supervisor<br/>breakdown · 14 items<br/><br/>prev = a3f1…<br/>hash = <b>7c02…</b>"]
        E3["<b>seq 3</b> · Continuity<br/>challenge filed<br/><br/>prev = 7c02…<br/>hash = <b>e918…</b>"]
        E4["<b>seq 4</b> · Counsel<br/>decision · pursue licence<br/><br/>prev = e918…<br/>hash = <b>2b44…</b>"]
        E1 --> E2 --> E3 --> E4
    end

    CANON["<b>canonicalJson()</b><br/>recursively sorted keys<br/><br/>postgres jsonb does not preserve key order.<br/>hash the naive JSON.stringify and every chain<br/>fails the moment it is read back from disk.<br/>this failure is silent."]
    CANON -.-> E2

    TRIG["<b>database trigger</b><br/>UPDATE → always refused<br/>DELETE → refused unless<br/>clearframe.allow_purge is set<br/>for the transaction"]
    TRIG -.-> chain

    TAMPER["someone with direct DB access<br/>disables the trigger and edits seq 2"]
    TAMPER --> BREAK["<b>verifyChain()</b> recomputes from stored rows<br/>→ { ok: false, brokenAt: 2 }<br/><br/>tampering is not merely discouraged.<br/>it is locatable to the exact entry."]

    E4 --> SIGN{"POST /reports/:id/sign"}
    SIGN -->|chain intact| OK["signed · head pinned<br/>at the moment of signature"]
    SIGN -->|chain broken| NO["409 · the ledger for this production<br/>is broken at entry N. it cannot be signed."]

